<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso García Robles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso García Robles was a Mexican diplomat who led the negotiations for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tlatelolco">Treaty of Tlatelolco</a> of 1967, which made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a> a nuclear-weapon-free zone. He later served as foreign minister and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>'s representative to the Committee on Disarmament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. He shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1982 with Alva Myrdal for his work on disarmament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-garcia-robles.jpg" alt="Alfonso García Robles" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcel Antonisse · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfonso_Garcia_Robles_1981.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
